rules:
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All decisions must be expressed using a structured YAML decision schema
    rather than unstructured narrative text to enable machine processing and UI rendering.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture decisions must be recorded and updated only in decision records
    (ADR); all other representations must be derived from ADR to prevent inconsistencies.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All patterns must be created as supporting by default and never directly
    as core to ensure validation through evidence before becoming foundational.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Patterns must not be merged or consolidated across different architectural
    layers to preserve separation between governance, execution, and reliability concerns.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Defines the precedence model: Global Rules > Project Rules > Prompt Rules.
    Higher-precedence rules act as hard constraints and cannot be overridden.'
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All heuristic-derived patterns must include at least one linked signal
    as evidence to ensure grounding in observed behaviour.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures consistent interpretation between pattern maturity (knowledge evolution)
    and decision status (governance lifecycle).
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Signals are eligible for pattern promotion only if they satisfy mandatory
    criteria: Recurrence, System Impact, Reusability, and Stability.'
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts (AEM, AID, Alignment Reports) summarize
    authoritative sources and must not become authoritative sources themselves.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Workflows must comply with the CAS Execution Model, separating reasoning
    from orchestration and knowledge access, while consuming context from CAS Runner.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The lifecycle stage of any architecture item must be derived from its decision
    status; items not marked 'accepted' cannot be marked as DONE.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects must participate in a shared Knowledge Workspace and avoid duplicating
    existing global governance structures.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work is the authoritative source of planning state; generated
    artifacts must derive status from it to ensure roadmap consistency.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The Architecture Evolution Map (AEM) must remain consistent with and never
    contradict decisions recorded in ADRs.
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Maintains human-in-the-loop control; all decisions proposed by the system
    must be explicitly accepted, rejected, or deferred by an architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must be persisted as structured ADRs before
    being reflected in the AEM or other derived artifacts.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns must represent foundational primitives rather than specific
    implementation strategies or replaceable approaches.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Promotion of patterns to 'core' status requires strong evidence from multiple
    sources or systems to ensure architectural stability.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines semantic contracts for language in artifacts, distinguishing between
    Intent and State, and Decisions vs System State.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
